.\" Manpage for archive_all.sh
.TH ARCHIVE_ALL 1 "August 2024" "1.0" "Bash Scripts"
.SH NAME
archive_all.sh \- Archive and optionally encrypt files in the current directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B archive_all.sh
[<I>password</I>]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B archive_all.sh
script archives all files in the current directory, optionally encrypting them with OpenSSL if a password is provided.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B tar
.TP
.B openssl
.SH USAGE
To archive files:
.PP
.B ./archive_all.sh [password]
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 if an error occurs.
.SH AUTHOR
AnAnnoyinGoose

